0.8.4

<Step id="STEP_3B_TOOL_API">
      <Goal>`config` kind only: verify the CURRENT API of every third-party tool this phase configures (`AX_THIRD_PARTY_TOOL_CURRENT_API`). Any other kind skips this step.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Per tool, BEFORE writing any config:
        1. Installed version: read `<modules-dir>/<pkg>/package.json` field `version`.
        2. Local CHANGELOG (recent major + previous): look for `BREAKING`, `deprecated`, `removed`, `migration`.
        3. Local README: current-version config syntax.
        4. Local docs minimal → WebFetch homepage from `package.json#homepage` / `repository.url`.
        5. Network blocked AND local docs insufficient → `H_THIRD_PARTY_API_UNVERIFIABLE` — halt rather
           than guess or apply a training-default silently.
        This four-step read (`package.json` version, CHANGELOG, README, homepage) is the FULL extent
        of local-package inspection this step performs. Reverse-engineering a tool's internal
        schema/config-shape files under `node_modules` (a bundled `configuration_schema.json`,
        minified source, internal type declarations) is not a step in this protocol — the concrete
        config specifics this phase needs (exact version, config-schema version/URL, a literal
        config skeleton, known version gotchas) are a decision-time infra-spec responsibility
        (`AX_RESEARCH_PERSISTED`, `infra.directive` STEP_3_TOOL_CHOICES), sourced from the ticket's
        Spec Refs or a linked research document, never reconstructed here by archaeology through
        package internals. When the ticket / spec / research does not already carry what this phase
        needs to write the config, that gap is `H_THIRD_PARTY_API_UNVERIFIABLE` (surfaced as
        `H_BLOCKED` to the operator per `AX_BLOCKER_ESCALATION`) — never a cue to keep digging
        through `node_modules` for it.
        Then log via `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> line "verified <tool>@<version> <one-line
        summary>" --phase <PhaseID>` (`AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE`) — audit requires this entry per config artifact.
      </Action>
    </Step>